st_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d30288f819fbd3ce96dd7082873555136e0a8ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/5d30288f819fbd3ce96dd7082873555136e0a8ac","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/5d30288f819fbd3ce96dd7082873555136e0a8ac"}]},{"sha":"21be16eacb992bcef54c13449fc36d0f4954c0a9","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTYyNTYxNDQ6MjFiZTE2ZWFjYjk5MmJjZWY1NGMxMzQ0OWZjMzZkMGY0OTU0YzBhOQ==","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sean Curtis","email":"sean.curtis@tri.global","date":"2021-07-07T17:02:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2021-07-07T17:02:49Z"},"message":"[geometry] Replace collision filter legacy for collision filter (breaking) (#15297)\n\n* Replace collision filter legacy for collision filter (breaking)\n\nWe're changing the under-the-hood implementation of collision filters.\nRemoving CollisionFilterLegacy has the following further implications:\n\n  - Existing API on GeometryState has been re-expressed in terms of the new\n    collision filter mechanism.\n  - ProximityEngine has entirely lost its collision filtering logic. It now\n    relies on the CollisionFilter class to do \"apply\" declarations.\n  - (Breaking) The \"sorted vectors have intersection\" supporting code in\n    the common directory is no longer used. Removing it is *technically*\n    a breaking change, but it's code that never really belonged in common\n    and is *highly* unlikely to be used by anyone else, ever.\n  - All explicit references to \"cliques\" are removed\n    - InternalFrame no longer tracks \"frame cliques\"\n    - Testing is no longer expressed in terms of cliques.\n    - GeometryState and ProximityEngine have lost clique-related APIs.\n    - Removal of the attorney between geometry state and collision filters.\n  - All callbacks that were dependent on CollisionFilterLegacy get touched.\n    (This represents roughly two thirds of the changed files).\n    - Their declared type has changed.\n    - They no longer operate on EncodedData::encoding(), but on id().","tree":{"sha":"aa85cd2746d77f2a79bce4a07982efcd0e477f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/trees/aa85cd2746d77f2a79bce4a07982efcd0e477f2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/commits/21be16eacb992bcef54c13449fc36d0f4954c0a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJg5d45CRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAOVsIAFW0wcYKejuNObTVSlSg7OrB\nfRJ7P1eFPN/FZXQBogDRUeJAn3A7dayCX/8XREaUHO4Eslqkqld88kTL81KQMEy3\nL0qf8IxEAgJEAoEI0hlVcMnRaKD7R+8I1lRbL4PdhjKf3+035P1LnWphvfblZrRN\n2pdqu6m8IQgAnRT7Dg6oWK9gpNuk5gIoIaSGfYm5b7AG7TWbHjGsSJYKYGNzJ1sX\ngQ1+sE0taHvckRIrftsrqk89wTdBgjz0Q55bwCu6oZWO4ID0xa41ubgIntvbVM34\ndHVTybnyfyR2ATEmZMJAl3THfuUdxXoG1MP7o3ffw2SX2fIrqyAxKyUwDV2WVGw=\n=bvGW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa85cd2746d77f2a79bce4a07982efcd0e477f2d\nparent 9427958a78d8fe32a6be6e4bfc1532941d70a2a1\nauthor Sean Curtis <sean.curtis@tri.global> 1625677369 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1625677369 -0400\n\n[geometry] Replace collision filter legacy for collision filter (breaking) (#15297)\n\n* Replace collision filter legacy for collision filter (breaking)\n\nWe're changing the under-the-hood implementation of collision filters.\nRemoving CollisionFilterLegacy has the following further implications:\n\n  - Existing API on GeometryState has been re-expressed in terms of the new\n    collision filter mechanism.\n  - ProximityEngine has entirely lost its collision filtering logic. It now\n    relies on the CollisionFilter class to do \"apply\" declarations.\n  - (Breaking) The \"sorted vectors have intersection\" supporting code in\n    the common directory is no longer used. Removing it is *technically*\n    a breaking change, but it's code that never really belonged in common\n    and is *highly* unlikely to be used by anyone else, ever.\n  - All explicit references to \"cliques\" are removed\n    - InternalFrame no longer tracks \"frame cliques\"\n    - Testing is no longer expressed in terms of cliques.\n    - GeometryState and ProximityEngine have lost clique-related APIs.\n    - Removal of the attorney between geometry state and collision filters.\n  - All callbacks that were dependent on CollisionFilterLegacy get touched.\n    (This represents roughly two thirds of the changed files).\n    - Their declared type has changed.\n    - They no longer operate on EncodedData::encoding(), but on id().\n","verified_at":"2024-01-16T19:59:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/21be16eacb992bcef54c13449fc36d0f4954c0a9","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/21be16eacb992bcef54c13449fc36d0f4954c0a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/21be16eacb992bcef54c13449fc36d0f4954c0a9/comments","author":{"login":"SeanCurtis-TRI","id":22159799,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTU5Nzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22159799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI","html_url":"https://github.com/SeanCurtis-TRI","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9427958a78d8fe32a6be6e4bfc1532941d70a2a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/9427958a78d8fe32a6be6e4bfc1532941d70a2a1","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/9427958a78d8fe32a6be6e4bfc1532941d70a2a1"}]},{"sha":"040c1e3af2de1b60131285150a614536cca4132c","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTYyNTYxNDQ6MDQwYzFlM2FmMmRlMWI2MDEzMTI4NTE1MGE2MTQ1MzZjY2E0MTMyYw==","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Nimmer","email":"jeremy.nimmer@tri.global","date":"2021-06-29T00:41:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2021-06-29T00:41:00Z"},"message":"[common] Add explicit function template instantiation macro on scalars (#15218)\n\nPort several different kinds of call sites to use it, as a demonstration\r\nof sufficiency and correctness.","tree":{"sha":"d961e11666578e8e4eb7ab3ae6f251cf57663c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/trees/d961e11666578e8e4eb7ab3ae6f251cf57663c7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/commits/040c1e3af2de1b60131285150a614536cca4132c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJg2mwcCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAA2GkIAF994txj7kK88xpJwUNoO336\nIBJkii5rX54gVWdUuCqEpzzMFJpvZl7OoknuGMT3KLoIW4/O9JUjylNScwTmvHTP\nuVDmLo0AFhs6TQwAao1Pf/OUkIpWu2GPfEaUI+53A/m3wZJxHnyWVN6NcjlhBUQH\nDjglRQlxO6Un4FktWmkeLgUPyroWz6ZgWO8bGitJoaPK+mrVAKigd3A1wwjRNcnT\nq1d8AF3eMdz4gwlfFttDaUlhkrKF3IKwUS98j1KoG3Ceh7zQzYNd6K0/8ICxu1YB\n5PlXgPwaIY/rA23x6fyEm5WD4OqcdQm9QpTIaYBLWRFyQ0+yQ9crCEEVy2gByOQ=\n=aKcQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d961e11666578e8e4eb7ab3ae6f251cf57663c7f\nparent ffffec45b95f5ef76471331ce60394778d345e57\nauthor Jeremy Nimmer <jeremy.nimmer@tri.global> 1624927260 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1624927260 -0700\n\n[common] Add explicit function template instantiation macro on scalars (#15218)\n\nPort several different kinds of call sites to use it, as a demonstration\r\nof sufficiency and correctness.","verified_at":"2024-01-16T19:59:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/040c1e3af2de1b60131285150a614536cca4132c","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/040c1e3af2de1b60131285150a614536cca4132c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/040c1e3af2de1b60131285150a614536cca4132c/comments","author":{"login":"jwnimmer-tri","id":17596505,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTk2NTA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17596505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri","html_url":"https://github.com/jwnimmer-tri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwnimmer-tri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ffffec45b95f5ef76471331ce60394778d345e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/ffffec45b95f5ef76471331ce60394778d345e57","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/ffffec45b95f5ef76471331ce60394778d345e57"}]},{"sha":"8205d935f3e2b024646f94d011b833dc4f21e900","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTYyNTYxNDQ6ODIwNWQ5MzVmM2UyYjAyNDY0NmY5NGQwMTFiODMzZGM0ZjIxZTkwMA==","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sean Curtis","email":"sean.curtis@tri.global","date":"2021-04-12T23:34:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2021-04-12T23:34:56Z"},"message":"[geometry] Deprecate the \"is grad unique\" flag from query results (#14875)\n\nThe flag reporting whether the gradient is unique had several problems:\n  1. It wasn't always valid (box and cylinder ignored questions of\n     uniqueness when the query point was *inside*).\n  2. That information alone is not particularly actionable; it\n     would be better to know the full space of valid vectors.\n  3. We have no code that actually makes use of this classifier\n     (and no optimization code that even *can*).\n\nTherefore, we're not computing it correctly, not using it, and\nhave no plans to do so, we'll simplify the code by deprecating and\nthen removing this flag.\n\nThe tests in proximitiy_engine_test are inherently redundant of the tests\nfor the callback directly. These test haven't be triaged and culled yet,\nbut for the purpose of this deprecation, it simply won't pay attention to\nwhether or not the gradient is unique or not.\n\nNOTE: The python bindings for the query result never bound the\nboolean flag, means no deprecation effort is necessary in the\nbindings.\n\n* Deprecating vector is unique in SignedDistancePair\n\nDeprecate SignedDistancePair::is_nhat_BA_W_unique\n\nThis follows logically from the deprecation of\nSignedDistanceToPoint::is_grad_W_unique.\n\nThere are a couple of differences compared to the\nSigndDistanceToPoint deprecation.\n - is_nhat_BA_W_unique was bound in python bindings, so this\n   includes deprecations in the bindings as well.\n - SignedDistancePair had a weird constructor that only existed\n   for tests. Rather than trying to maintain a version into the\n   future, the tests were reformulated so that the constructor\n   is no longer called and it can simply be deprecated in\n   anticipation of simple removal.","tree":{"sha":"e0f67d018cfa3bce33eb83b96238b1c6666aa276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/trees/e0f67d018cfa3bce33eb83b96238b1c6666aa276"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/git/commits/8205d935f3e2b024646f94d011b833dc4f21e900","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJgdNkgCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAdHIIAGzNzNJCqbdiZON3scgKqQU5\nAox0dE/QkH/VGkKyVYCv6ngtfFYxsvuR6X3kcCEfrlvyqG8i9vFbJYEgnxD7o2Ti\n0bc8h33jsnoGlj2GDSg63r5syM08FrEOzZxfaCEPyB8pIgZJw7nEJs1vIonfXu0O\nOp5PBXuoKAc3WM5byazTCGa3R6hudDmLNGINv7iThESekruEPPinuYdNbq2bofkm\nr69jMKYvRQSe0T0IR+wEVEqDN3NX5n1b3K4j4R/41lJWnUzKQL/KLStWmwK0EWZh\nvnWknT4SYDeGI1FdEWV3PasWTkXYNArvQYTEdn+NZpAPq47ENNvtp+ZVGtOL1zc=\n=s3aP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e0f67d018cfa3bce33eb83b96238b1c6666aa276\nparent ec769b1ce5611d7e992a911cfb7857963a2fa69e\nauthor Sean Curtis <sean.curtis@tri.global> 1618270496 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1618270496 -0700\n\n[geometry] Deprecate the \"is grad unique\" flag from query results (#14875)\n\nThe flag reporting whether the gradient is unique had several problems:\n  1. It wasn't always valid (box and cylinder ignored questions of\n     uniqueness when the query point was *inside*).\n  2. That information alone is not particularly actionable; it\n     would be better to know the full space of valid vectors.\n  3. We have no code that actually makes use of this classifier\n     (and no optimization code that even *can*).\n\nTherefore, we're not computing it correctly, not using it, and\nhave no plans to do so, we'll simplify the code by deprecating and\nthen removing this flag.\n\nThe tests in proximitiy_engine_test are inherently redundant of the tests\nfor the callback directly. These test haven't be triaged and culled yet,\nbut for the purpose of this deprecation, it simply won't pay attention to\nwhether or not the gradient is unique or not.\n\nNOTE: The python bindings for the query result never bound the\nboolean flag, means no deprecation effort is necessary in the\nbindings.\n\n* Deprecating vector is unique in SignedDistancePair\n\nDeprecate SignedDistancePair::is_nhat_BA_W_unique\n\nThis follows logically from the deprecation of\nSignedDistanceToPoint::is_grad_W_unique.\n\nThere are a couple of differences compared to the\nSigndDistanceToPoint deprecation.\n - is_nhat_BA_W_unique was bound in python bindings, so this\n   includes deprecations in the bindings as well.\n - SignedDistancePair had a weird constructor that only existed\n   for tests. Rather than trying to maintain a version into the\n   future, the tests were reformulated so that the constructor\n   is no longer called and it can simply be deprecated in\n   anticipation of simple removal.\n","verified_at":"2024-01-16T19:59:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/8205d935f3e2b024646f94d011b833dc4f21e900","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/8205d935f3e2b024646f94d011b833dc4f21e900","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/8205d935f3e2b024646f94d011b833dc4f21e900/comments","author":{"login":"SeanCurtis-TRI","id":22159799,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTU5Nzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22159799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI","html_url":"https://github.com/SeanCurtis-TRI","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeanCurtis-TRI/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ec769b1ce5611d7e992a911cfb7857963a2fa69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/commits/ec769b1ce5611d7e992a911cfb7857963a2fa69e","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/commit/ec769b1ce5611d7e992a911cfb7857963a2fa69e"}]}]